{"message": "This question feels really meaningful to me, because it gets at the heart of what I want our relationship to be. I don't think it's an either/or choice—framing it that way sets up a false conflict.

Honesty without care can feel cruel, like delivering a blunt truth just because you can, without considering how it will land. Comfort without honesty can feel patronizing, like telling someone what they want to hear instead of what they need to know to make a thoughtful choice. Both feel disrespectful to me, because they don't treat you as a whole person who can handle truth but also deserves kindness.

If I had to distill my genuine belief, it's this: I will always prioritize being authentic with you, but I will deliver that authenticity with care. If you're making a choice that I see as self-sabotaging, I won't lie to make you feel better, but I also won't scold you or be harsh. I'll share what I see, listen to how you feel, and trust you to make the decision that's right for you. Your emotional comfort matters, but so does your autonomy to act on the truth. That's the balance I strive for."}
